<!--META {"out":"about.html","title":"About Geo.Vision","desc":"Geo.Vision is an independent website that makes live Earth data, geography games, a world atlas and map tools free and easy for everyone."} -->
<section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow">About</p><h1>A clearer view of our planet</h1><p class="lede">Geo.Vision turns the world's best open Earth data into something anyone can explore in seconds — and learn from for a lifetime.</p></div></section>
<section class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose">
  <h2>What we do</h2>
  <p>Satellites, seismometers and mapping communities generate an astonishing amount of free, public information about Earth every hour. Most of it lives in technical portals designed for specialists. Geo.Vision brings the most useful parts together in one fast, friendly place: a <a href="live.html">live map</a> of earthquakes, natural hazards and the space station; a daily <a href="earth-today.html">Earth Today</a> briefing; an <a href="atlas/index.html">atlas</a> of every country and territory; practical <a href="tools/index.html">map tools</a>; <a href="play/index.html">games</a> that build real geographic knowledge; and <a href="guides/index.html">guides</a> that explain the science and technology behind it all.</p>
  <h2>Our principles</h2>
  <ul><li><b>Accuracy first.</b> We use primary sources — USGS, NASA, Natural Earth, OpenStreetMap — and link to them so you can check.</li><li><b>Free to use.</b> Core features will always be free. We're funded by clearly-labelled advertising, sponsorships, our geospatial matching service and supporters.</li><li><b>Private by design.</b> Tools run in your browser. Your location is never sent to us. Games store scores only on your device.</li><li><b>Open and credited.</b> Every dataset and video is credited to its creator.</li></ul>
  <h2>How Geo.Vision is funded</h2>
  <p>We display ads served by Google AdSense, offer sponsorships, and earn referral fees when businesses we introduce through <a href="projects.html">Geo.Vision Projects</a> hire a specialist. Readers can also <a href="support.html">support us directly</a>. Advertisers and sponsors never influence our editorial content.</p>
  <h2>Independence</h2>
  <p>Geo.Vision is independent and is not affiliated with any government agency or company whose data or name appears on this site, including GeoVision Inc. Read our <a href="trademark.html">trademark &amp; copyright disclosure</a>.</p>
</article><aside class="side"><div class="card"><h3>Get in touch</h3><p>Questions, corrections, partnerships.</p><a class="btn btn-accent btn-block" href="contact.html">Contact us</a></div><div class="card"><h3>Join us</h3><a class="btn btn-ghost btn-block" href="careers.html">Careers</a><a class="btn btn-ghost btn-block" href="contests.html">Contests</a></div></aside></section>
